  "id": "scopolamine",
  "term": "scopolamine",
  "definition": "Scopolamine is a plant-derived drug from the nightshade family that blocks acetylcholine activity at muscarinic receptors. It has anticholinergic effects and is used to reduce motion-related nausea and dizziness, decrease some body secretions, slow gut movement, and dilate the pupils.",
